From 7589fd81f8ca1c99cf00da0fefc62125aae4a132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Dirson <yann.dirson@vates.tech>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:16:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] init: wait up to 120s for the network to come online

reloadNetwork() waits at most 20s for systemd-networkd-wait-online,
then goes on (it only logs the timeout).  At init time (when the
network is configured by boot command-line, fetching the answerfile or
the answerfile_generator script was done only once, without retry. On
hardware where link negotiation plus DHCP takes longer, the fetch
fails with "Unable to fetch script ...": on a phoenixNAP s1.c1.small
(dual 10G Intel NICs), network-online took about 1 min.

systemd-networkd-wait-online returns as soon as the network is up, so
a longer limit costs nothing on fast networks.

This change does not modify the reloadNetwork default timeout, so in
interactive mode the user does not have to wait for 2min if the
timeout is caused by a config error.  The ability to retry present
there is already sufficient.

Originally-by: Olivier Lambert <olivier.lambert@vates.tech>
Signed-off-by: Yann Dirson <yann.dirson@vates.tech>
---
 init | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init b/init
index a1789f6..71d305d 100755
--- a/init
+++ b/init
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ def configureNetworking(ui, device, config):
         netcfg[i].writeSystemdNetworkdConfig(i)
 
     # Reload network to apply the configuration
-    netutil.reloadNetwork()
+    netutil.reloadNetwork(timeout=120)
 
     if ui:
         ui.progress.clearModelessDialog()
